.TH ESDM\-KERNEL\-SEEDER 8 "2026-08-05" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-kernel\-seeder \- periodically seed the Linux kernel RNG from the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-kernel\-seeder
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-kernel\-seeder
draws random data from
.BR esdm\-server (8)
over the unprivileged RPC interface and inserts it into the Linux kernel RNG,
crediting it with entropy. It fills the role an
.BR rngd (8)
has for the kernel, but with the ESDM as the source.
.PP
This is required whenever the ESDM runs the interrupt entropy source, because
that source deprives the kernel RNG of its main entropy input. It is
worthwhile in every other configuration as well, since the kernel then also
benefits from the entropy sources only the ESDM has access to.
.PP
The daemon inserts data at start\-up and afterwards once per seeding interval.
Until the first insertion has succeeded it retries every two seconds instead
of waiting out the full interval, so that a freshly booted kernel is topped up
without delay. Data is handed to the CUSE device provided by
.BR esdm\-cuse\-random (8)
if it is present, and to
.I /dev/random
directly otherwise.
.PP
.B esdm\-kernel\-seeder
must be started as root, as inserting entropy into the kernel requires the
.B CAP_SYS_ADMIN
capability. On systemd installations it is normally started through the
shipped
.B esdm\-kernel\-seeder.service
unit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " \fISECS\fR"
Seconds between two seeding operations. A non\-numeric argument is rejected.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbosity
Increase the logging verbosity. May be given repeatedly.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-syslog
Log to syslog instead of standard output and standard error.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-force\-pr
Draw the data from the prediction\-resistance generator of the ESDM, and force
a reseed of the kernel CRNG right after every insertion. This mode is selected
automatically when the ESDM was built for the AIS 20/31 NTG.1 seeding
strategy.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT ", " SIGQUIT ", " SIGHUP
Terminate the daemon. The pending sleep between two seeding operations is
interrupted, so the shutdown does not wait for the interval to expire.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-cuse\-random (8),
.BR esdm\-tool (1),
.BR random (4)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephan Mueller <smueller@chronox.de>
